{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:13GraphProducts13TensorProductV","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TensorProduct"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TensorProduct"}],"title":"TensorProduct","modules":[{"name":"GraphProducts"}],"role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"TensorProduct.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct.swift#L42"}},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct"},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/Position","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/UndirectedEdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/UndirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/UndirectedIndexRow"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/first","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/second"]},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/Graph-Implementations"]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The tensor product G × H of two graphs, both directed or both undirected, as a lazy view. Made","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tensorProduct(_:_:)"},{"text":". Also called the direct, categorical or Kronecker product.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TensorProduct"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"First"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Second"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices and their indices are as in "},{"code":"CartesianProduct","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The row of (g, h) lists "},{"code":"(g′, h′)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each entry g′ of G’s row of g and each entry h′ of H’s row of h, G outer. Rows are computed from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the factors’ index rows and never hash."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An edge’s position is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position(first: e, second: f, reversed:)"},{"text":": G’s edge ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e"},{"text":" and H’s edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"text":". In an undirected product two non-loop edges {a, b} and {c, d} give two edges, the straight","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"{(a, c), (b, d)} and the reversed {(a, d), (b, c)}, where a, c are the edges’ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"u"},{"text":" ends; when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"either is a self-loop they coincide and there is one, not reversed. A row lists a factor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop from its first appearance only, so every product edge has each of its ends once in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the rows. Directed, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reversed"},{"text":" is always false, and the product has edge indices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"index(e)·m_H + index(f)"},{"text":" when both factors have them; undirected it has none, because a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop changes how many edges a factor pair gives.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphproducts\/tensorproduct"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://GraphProducts/documentation/GraphProducts/TensorProduct/DirectedEdges":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedEdges","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphproducts\/tensorproduct\/directededges","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice"